    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nBeachfront home in a very desirable area\n\nSet on approximately 2.47 acres of beautifully maintained gardens and grassland, this exceptional five-bedroom residence offers a rare opportunity to enjoy coastal living at its very best. Extending to approximately 319.8 sq. m., the property combines generous family accommodation, breath-taking water and mountain views, and direct access to one of the region's most sought-after beaches.\n\nDesigned with flexibility in mind, the home is ideally suited to a large family and/or multi-generational living, featuring five well-proportioned bedrooms (three ensuite) including two bedrooms located on the ground floor. The bright and spacious kitchen/dining area enjoys spectacular sea views, creating the perfect setting for everyday living and entertaining. Additional accommodation includes a sitting room, a separate living room, a conservatory overlooking the coastline, an office looking over the mountains, a utility room, guest WC, a family bathroom and a shower room. \n\nOutside, the property is surrounded by expansive lawns, with far-reaching sea views to the rear and stunning mountain views to the front. A detached garage with running water offers further potential and may be suitable for conversion, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\n\nOne of the property's most outstanding features is its direct access to the sandy shores of the Blue Flag Templetown Beach, renowned for its pristine waters and natural beauty. Whether enjoying long beach walks, water sports, or simply relaxing in peaceful surroundings, this home offers an enviable lifestyle where nature and comfort meet.\n\nDespite its tranquil setting, the property benefits from excellent connectivity, with easy access to the M1 motorway and Dublin Airport, while Dundalk, Dublin, and Belfast are all within convenient reach. This unique location provides the perfect combination of coastal serenity and modern accessibility.\n\nAdditional features include oil-fired central heating, a septic tank system, and broadband connectivity, ensuring comfortable year-round living in this exceptional seaside home."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Well-appointed family accommodation set on approx. 2.47 acres of land</li><li>Bright open plan living areas with spectacular views</li><li>Rural yet accessible location</li><li>Panoramic sea and mountain views in one of the region's most sought-after locations.</li><li>Detached garage, with potential for conversion, subject to the necessary planning permissions.</ul>"
